of_node_put(nchangeset);
...
unittest(of_property_present(parent, "prop-remove"), ...);
ret = of_property_read_string(parent, "prop-update", &propstr);
Reason:
The variable `parent` is aliased to `nchangeset`, both pointing to the same `struct device_node`. Calling `of_node_put(nchangeset)` can drop the reference count to zero and free the node. Subsequent uses of `parent` in `of_property_present()` and `of_property_read_string()` access freed memory, causing a use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
unittest(of_property_present(parent, "prop-remove"), ...);
ret = of_property_read_string(parent, "prop-update", &propstr);
...
of_node_put(nchangeset);
Reason:
Moving `of_node_put(nchangeset)` after all accesses to `parent` ensures the device node is still valid when its properties are checked and read. This prevents prematurely freeing the node while it is still in use.

